      "content": "If you're tired of the performance, then the most honest thing you can do is stop trying to be someone you're not. Trying to fix a fundamental flaw is a Sisyphean task; you'll just end up exhausted again. True honesty might be accepting that you are broken, and then finding a way to let that brokenness simply *be*, without the pressure of having to pretend otherwise. It's a quiet surrender, not a failure.",
